          "A14": {
            "value": "Asian Paints exhibits a minimal EV-to-Equity bridge of ~0.4%, reflecting a lean balance sheet with modest net debt (₹125 cr is <0.1% of EV). Minority interests and associates add <₹1,000 cr combined, typical for a consolidated player with strong operating cash generation. This tight bridge signals financial discipline and low leverage — a structural strength. Across scenarios, target prices range from ₹1,017 (Bear) to ₹1,757 (Bull), with Base case at ₹1,382. All three scenarios imply 35–65% downside versus the current market price of ₹2,920, pointing to a substantial gap between DCF value and market consensus. This divergence likely stems from two sources: (1) conservative DCF assumptions — perpetual growth of 5% may be too low given paints category tailwinds and Asian Paints' 18% ROE; WACC of 11.65% may be elevated if true equity risk premium is closer to 5–5.5% rather than 6%; (2) market is implicitly pricing long-run margin expansion and volume growth at the upper bound of defensibility, possibly 6–7% perpetual growth with stable 15%+ RoIC. The SELL recommendation is mechanically justified but warrants sensitivity testing on g and WACC before publication; a 50–75 bps reduction in perpetual g or 100 bps drop in WACC would materially lift targets and shift recommendation to HOLD or BUY, closing much of the gap to market. Given valuation risk and model uncertainty at this magnitude, an analyst review of terminal assumptions and peer-relative metrics is essential.",
